# The build context is the repo root (see stack/Containerfile), because the image gate
# imports `qd_train.tristate` and a stack/-only context cannot reach `python/`.
#
# A root context would otherwise ship 1.5 GB of Rust build output to the daemon on every
# build, so the exclusions below are what keep that context small. Measured before this
# file existed: target/ 1.5 GB, .venv/ 120 MB, against python/ at 1.7 MB.

# Rust build output — by far the largest thing in the tree, and never needed in the image.
target/

# The Mac-local Python environment. The image builds its own venv from the lockfile; copying
# this one in would put aarch64/macOS wheels inside a linux/amd64 image.
.venv/

# Repo state and tooling caches.
.git/
.gitignore
.pytest_cache/
.devmap/
.DS_Store

# Evidence and records. These are the audit trail, not build inputs — and AUDIT/ holds build
# logs, so including it would make each build's context depend on the previous build's output.
AUDIT/
HANDOFF/
ledger/
gaps.jsonl

# Documentation.
docs/
README.md
LICENSE

# Rust sources. Kernel work lands in ~/Code/research/tessl and the runtime crates are built
# on the host, not in this image.
crates/
Cargo.toml
Cargo.lock

# Test fixtures and dev tooling.
fixtures/
tools/
python/tests/
